&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Make is the platform to manage all your automations and AI agents in one visual landscape – for teams driving business impact without relying on developers. Part of Celonis, a global leader in process intelligence recognized on the Forbes Cloud 100 for seven consecutive years, we&#39;re headquartered in Prague, Czechia, with hubs in Madrid, Munich, Raleigh, and Pristina, and teams across the UK, France, India, and the Netherlands, among other locations.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a highly motivated and technically strong Product Manager to lead the team that owns where Make keeps what a company knows.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;That is two products. &lt;strong&gt;Make Knowledge&lt;/strong&gt; connects a company&#39;s documents, policies, and procedures so that people and AI agents can find the right answer — and see where it came from.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Make Tables&lt;/strong&gt; is our database product, being rebuilt from the ground up so that anyone can store and work with business data without writing code. Together they are what every automation, every AI agent, and every person working in Make relies on to get the facts right. As companies hand more of their work to AI, the hard part is no longer building something — it is trusting what it did. This role owns the products that make that trust possible.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape the product strategy and roadmap for Knowledge and Tables as one connected product, so that people, automations, and AI agents all work from the same trusted information.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take Make Knowledge from its current closed Beta to general availability — validating with real customer teams that it solves a problem worth paying for, prioritizing the integrations that matter most, and landing how we package and price it.&lt;/li&gt;
